    "subHeader": "Launch your Ireland company with Arnifi to access EU markets, benefit from low corporate taxes, and operate seamlessly within a globally trusted regulatory environment\n",
    "blogs": [],
    "overviewDetail": "Ireland has established itself as one of the most attractive business destinations in Europe, offering direct access to the EU single market combined with a competitive tax regime. As a member of the European Union and the Eurozone, Ireland provides businesses with stability, regulatory transparency, and seamless trade across Europe.\nThe country is particularly known for its thriving technology, pharmaceutical, and financial services sectors. Global corporations such as Google, Apple, and Meta have established significant operations here, leveraging IrelandΓÇÖs favourable corporate tax policies and highly skilled workforce.\n\nIrelandΓÇÖs corporate tax rate of 12.5% continues to be a key driver for foreign investment, although recent global tax reforms have introduced a 15% minimum tax for large multinational enterprises. Despite this, Ireland remains highly competitive due to its strong infrastructure, access to talent, and business-friendly policies.\n\nWith robust legal protections, EU alignment, and a strong reputation for ease of doing business, Ireland is an ideal base for startups, SMEs, and multinational companies looking to scale across Europe and beyond.\n",
